  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "At a certain temperature, the degrees of freedom per molecule for gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>. The gas performs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of work when it expands under constant pressure. The amount of heat absorbed by the gas will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "750",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>For constant pressure process,</p><p>Work done is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is gas constant.</p><p>Now, for above process,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>.</p><p>So, specific heat at constant pressure is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>R</mi></math>.</p><p>Amount of heat adsorbed by the gas is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mi>R</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>150</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>750</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
